    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556-a1">

                <pb facs="0972" n="872" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg872"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 188.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoffman to Prince Gortchakoff</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 16–28,
                            1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prince</hi>: I have the honor to forward to your
                    highness, herewith, an autograph letter from the President of the United States
                    to His Majesty the Emperor, on the occasion of the 25th anniversary of his
                    accession to the throne, together with an office copy of the same.</p>
                <p>I am instructed by Mr. Evarts to take the first proper occasion to give
                    expression to the sentiments of regard and esteem towards His Majesty
                    entertained by the Government and people of the United States, and the interest
                    felt there in the important and memorable anniversary which is about to be
                    celebrated in Russia.</p>
                <p>Will your highness kindly convey the expression of these sentiments to His
                    Majesty the Emperor.</p>
                <p>I take, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WICKHAM HOFFMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
